**Security decisions made:**
1. AWS credentials only in server runtime (`.env`, never `NEXT_PUBLIC_`)
2. Presigned URLs for direct browser→S3 upload (no server bandwidth bottleneck)
3. File type/size validated server-side before presigning
4. Keys prefixed with `userId` + timestamp; path traversal sanitized
5. RLS policies on `files` table enforce ownership at DB layer
6. Session via `HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite` cookie (JWT in `jose`)
7. Structured Pino logging with redaction for secrets/headers
8. CSP-ready: no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, no inline scripts
9. Exact dependency versions pinned; lockfile committed
